Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/D-creek/meshcore-tdoa-gateway
Description: MeshCore TDOA USB-to-MQTT bridge
 The core gateway service: reads each USB-attached MeshCore LoRa receiver's
 serial stream, parses the TDOA-extended frames (per-packet reception records
 with hardware-captured arrival timestamps, GPS quality, device telemetry) and
 republishes them to MQTT for the cloud collector. Also drives firmware OTA and
 an optional loopback TCP passthrough for companion-app access.
 .
 Ships with NO credentials. The per-gateway MQTT credentials are written to a
 root-only 0600 /etc/meshcore-tdoa-gateway/bridge.yaml at register time by the
 portal package's register script; the bridge only ever reads them. Portal-set
 fields (per-port role + tcp_passthrough) live in a separate portal-writable
 bridge-overrides.yaml, so the unprivileged portal can never write the secrets
 this root daemon reads. Pure Python; the same .deb installs on amd64, arm64,
 armhf and armv6. The postinst builds an isolated venv at
 /opt/meshcore-tdoa-gateway-bridge/venv.

